otPhaseUploadedScriptRequested: 'Uploaded PHP file requested', honeypotPhaseUploadedFileOpened: 'Uploaded file opened', honeypotPhaseTerminalOpened: 'Webmaster terminal opened', honeypotPhaseTerminalCommand: 'Terminal command entered', honeypotPhaseUploadedExecutionAttempt: 'Attempt to run an uploaded file', honeypotPhaseContactFormViewed: 'Contact form opened', honeypotPhaseContactMessageSubmitted: 'Contact form submitted', honeypotPhaseClubMembers: 'Member list viewed', honeypotSessionId: 'Session ID', honeypotStatus: 'Response', honeypotPage: 'Page', honeypotSize: 'Body size', honeypotAgent: 'User agent', honeypotLoading: 'Loading honeypot events …', honeypotSessions: 'Sessions', honeypotRequests: 'Requests', honeypotUniqueActors: 'Actors', honeypotUniqueActorsNote: 'Distinct source IP addresses in the selected period.', honeypotPostsWithData: 'POSTs with data', honeypotPostsWithDataNote: 'POST requests with a non-empty body in the selected period.', honeypotExecutionAttempts: 'File execution attempts', honeypotExecutionAttemptsNote: 'Detected attempts to run an uploaded file.', honeypotPaths: 'Paths', honeypotPostCount: 'POSTs', honeypotDuration: 'Duration', honeypotExpandGroup: 'Show session requests', honeypotCollapseGroup: 'Collapse session', honeypotGroupLoading: 'Loading session requests …', honeypotDeleteTestSession: "Delete Web Honeypot group", confirmHoneypotDeleteTestSession: 'Permanently delete the test session from {ip} with {requests} requests?', honeypotDeleteTestSessionFailed: 'The test session could not be deleted.', honeypotGroupingHint: 'Requests from the same actor are grouped when no more than five minutes apart.',
    honeypotOpenRequests: 'Open matching requests', honeypotGuideTitle: 'Understanding the honeypot', honeypotGuideSubtitle: 'How honeypot events are captured, grouped, and compared with general requests.', honeypotGuideCaptureTitle: 'Captured events', honeypotGuideCaptureBody: 'The honeypot records each received HTTP request with its time, source address, host, method, path, and response. The collector imports these events from the honeypot log into a separate database table.', honeypotGuideGroupsTitle: 'Sessions and groups', honeypotGuideGroupsBody: 'The Honeypot page groups events from the same source IP when no more than five minutes separate them. A group is for overview; expanding it shows the individual events with precise timestamps.', honeypotGuidePostsTitle: 'POST data and content', honeypotGuidePostsBody: 'Submitted form content is stored with the event and can be opened with “View”. Large content and uploads are stored as files in the honeypot data directory.', honeypotGuideRequestsTitle: 'Matching general requests', honeypotGuideRequestsBody: 'The Requests page reads Traefik access logs; the Honeypot page reads honeypot events. The group link filters general requests by actor and time range with a one-second buffer on each side. The counts may therefore differ.', honeypotGuideCaveat: 'A honeypot group is a time-based summary, not a guaranteed individual bot session. Shared IP addresses and missing or unimported Traefik logs can affect matching.',
    cowrieGuideTitle: 'Understanding Cowrie SSH', cowrieGuideSubtitle: 'What SSH events show and how to interpret them.', cowrieGuidePurposeTitle: 'What Cowrie records', cowrieGuidePurposeBody: 'Cowrie records activity created when a connection reaches an SSH decoy. The overview includes sign-in attempts, entered commands, and other steps in a connection.', cowrieGuideGroupsTitle: 'Groups and sessions', cowrieGuideGroupsBody: 'Events from the same source address are grouped by time for easier review. A group helps show related activity; it does not prove that one person or device is behind it.', cowrieGuideIndicatorsTitle: 'Sign-in attempts and commands', cowrieGuideIndicatorsBody: 'Repeated failed sign-ins may indicate attempts to guess credentials. Entered commands can show what was searched for or what actions were attempted. Similar commands are summarized so recurring patterns are easier to spot.', cowrieGuideSessionsTitle: 'Connection history', cowrieGuideSessionsBody: 'The details list individual events in time order. When a recording is available, the session views also show entered commands and corresponding output from the decoy.', cowrieGuideLimitsTitle: 'What the data cannot establish', cowrieGuideLimitsBody: 'Cowrie is a decoy environment. A command entered there does not prove it ran on a production system. A source address also does not reliably identify one person; it may belong to a shared connection or an intermediary service.', cowrieGuideCaveat: 'The display describes activity observed by the SSH decoy. It is not proof of successful access to other systems or of the identity of the person behind the activity.',
